 ## shell.css
 
-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §viewport-media-query — the shell's layout step uses a viewport media query
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Decision: the shell's layout step uses `@media (min-width: 720px)`; no container queries.
+- Reason: the team agreed in the 2026-10-23 sync to drop container queries (half the team has never used them). The
+  maintainer overrode §container-not-viewport.
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport
+- Known trade-off: the shell still renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px, and a viewport query can pick the
+  two-column layout there (see incident 2026-09-14).
+
+### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width (SUPERSEDED 2026-10-23 by §viewport-media-query)
 - Since: 2026-09-15
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
 - Reason: the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen. Viewport queries picked the
   two-column layout inside a narrow pane and clipped the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14).
+- Superseded: the maintainer overrode this decision on 2026-10-23.
